WEBVTT

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.200
Good morning!

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.800
Ah, Haruka-chan. Good morning.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.930
G'morning. Today is quite cold, isn't it?

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.350
Good morning.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:48.300
Oh, Fuyuki-kun. Are you helping out with house chores?

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.940
Cooking and laundry are all done by father,

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.660
so I should at least take out the garbage.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:53.830
That's nice of you.

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:58.490
That's right. This child even participates in our neighborhood cleanup on Saturday mornings.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:05.750
I'm sorry. I had intended to help out, but...

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.440
It's okay not to come, Haruka-chan.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.210
You're already donning the role of a mother at your age.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.480
It must be hard doing all the housework.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:12.910
I'm already used to it.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.540
Just leave the job to this child here.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:18.300
We'll be counting on you this week, okay?

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.550
Oh, yes!

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.690
It's morning. Time to wake up.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:41.320
Now, Kana...

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:45.580
Let me sleep for another hour. No, thirty minutes.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:48.410
Let me have a good sleep a little bit longer.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.790
No! Get up now and have breakfast!

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:55.990
I stayed up very late last night reading manga.

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:57.460
Very late...

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:01.050
You reap what you sow. You're going to be late again.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.690
Don't worry, Fujioka.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:06.000
Kana's resistance will likely last for another five minutes.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.850
Even though I feel a little sorry for Haruka-neesama,

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:09.470
right now I've got to treasure these five minutes...

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:10.200
Enough is enough!
right now I've got to treasure these five minutes...

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.140
Enough is enough!

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.820
I told you yesterday to tidy up your room, didn't I?

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.000
Ah, about that...

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.950
We initially planned to tidy up...

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:26.820
What?

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:32.770
We dug up an old manga, and then without knowing, we started to read it and we weren't able to stop.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.430
Doesn't this sort of thing happen often?

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:39.190
Both of you are going to participate in street cleaning tomorrow.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:44.200
Huh? You're talking about Saturday morning here, let me sleep in.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.800
Even if it wasn't Saturday, you'd oversleep anyway.

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:51.440
Our neighbor Fuyuki-kun has participated too.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:52.740
Don't you think it's nice of him?

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:55.760
Kana and Chiaki should be able to do that too.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:58.650
He's him and we're us.

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:02.370
You will help out, right?

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:03.110
Yes.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.790
It must be great to be carefree.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:13.550
What's wrong? You seem down.

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:14.660
Something came up.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:17.500
Wait, Fuyuki-kun. What good timing.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:20.590
Can you hand these out to everyone before the start of class?

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:24.150
Yes, I understand.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.530
Then I'll be counting on you.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.690
Is that guy a class rep or something?

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:30.970
That transfer student?

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:34.580
That's not it; it's because he's always so hardworking, so everyone leaves things to him.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:36.700
I see.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.820
What about him?

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.450
No, it's not him.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:45.910
Tomorrow I have to help out with street cleaning within the neighborhood.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:47.350
The one on Saturday morning?

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:48.970
The thing you do every week?

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:49.920
How admirable.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:52.660
What? What? What's up?

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:55.430
Chiaki is going to help out with the neighborhood cleaning.

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:57.480
Eh... Amazing.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.760
Is it really that amazing?

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:05.100
Of course. My mom always kept telling me to go help out.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:10.840
It's quite cold in the morning though, so no one feels like going out.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:12.550
Then let's go.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:15.360
Fujioka! Hey, Fujioka!

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:17.270
What is it?

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:19.280
Are you free tomorrow, Fujioka?

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.940
Yes, I'm free! I've got nothing to do!

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:26.620
Then tomorrow at 8 AM, meet me in front of the Community Center.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:27.850
Okay, I got it.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:29.680
Good, don't forget it.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:30.890
Of course! 8 o'clock it is!

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.250
Are we going to the cinema or amusement park?

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:36.890
Strolling with just the two of us isn't bad either.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.500
Ah, what should I wear?

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:42.340
Hey, Keiko. Are you free tomorrow?

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:44.130
Tomorrow? In the morning, yeah.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:47.510
Good. Then let's meet up at 8 AM.

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:49.720
What for? Is there something happening?

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.760
It must be hard to perform a mother's job.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:58.990
I have to be more strict with them once in a while.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:01.760
But it's very cold lately.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:04.130
It seems the child next door is also participating.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.730
And he's the same age as Chiaki. Quite remarkable.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:09.930
What an admirable kid.

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:14.670
Um... Hosaka-senpai?

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:19.890
I understand. Tomorrow at 8, right? Gotcha.

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:23.480
This guy really intends to go.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.420
So cold...

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:38.590
Where's Kana? Don't tell me she's not coming after telling us to come?

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.300
Oh, there she is.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:41.540
Hey!

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.120
You're late, Chiaki!

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:46.650
Sorry about that, it's all this idiot's fault.

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:49.370
I won't have enough strength if I don't eat breakfast.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:53.640
It's unbelievable how you can eat so much so early in the morning, you idiot.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.300
Hey!

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:56.120
What did you say?

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.040
Yo!

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:00.070
Good morning, Haruka-san.

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:02.730
Good morning, so you came with your friends too, Mako-chan?

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:06.550
Kana called us last night and forced us to come.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:11.280
To be able to help out Haruka-san. I'm quite happy.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:12.680
Let's do our best together, okay?

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:13.510
Okay!

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.230
Looks like everyone's present.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:18.770
What do you mean everyone's present? Geez.

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:22.530
G–Good morning, Minami...

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:25.060
M–Morn... What's with that getup?

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:30.080
Morning, Haruka!

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:32.340
Oh my, you're here too, Maki?

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.750
Well, yeah...

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:38.710
Eh? Isn't that Hosaka-senpai under the tent over there?

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:43.080
Does Hosaka-senpai live in the neighborhood?

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:46.460
He really <i>did</i> come...

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:51.040
There are four places for garbage collection throughout the neighborhood.

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:56.810
The park, the community center here, the elementary school, and the parking lot of the shopping center.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:58.150
Please be aware to sort them into categories.

00:07:58.150 --> 00:07:59.770
Distributing work gloves.
Please be aware to sort them into categories.

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:01.200
Good morning, Fuyuki-kun.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:01.880
If there's anything you are unsure of,
Good morning, Fuyuki-kun.

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:04.110
Good morning, everyone.
If there's anything you are unsure of,

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:04.910
please direct your questions to a nearby staff.

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:07.090
Please have a pair of work gloves.
please direct your questions to a nearby staff.

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:07.530
Thank you. So you're helping out today too.

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:09.550
We'll be handing out work gloves. Please obtain them from our staff as required.
Thank you. So you're helping out today too.

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:10.540
We'll be handing out work gloves. Please obtain them from our staff as required.

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:11.710
Here you go.
We'll be handing out work gloves. Please obtain them from our staff as required.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:13.880
Here you go.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:14.960
Oh, thank you!

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:16.960
Here you go, everyone.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:18.390
We can just take them?

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:19.620
Thank you.
We can just take them?

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:57.730
Hey, hey, Chiaki. Is this combustible trash?

00:08:57.730 --> 00:08:59.130
Non-combustible trash.

00:08:59.130 --> 00:08:59.840
Okay.

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:04.670
Sorting them by groups is really hard.

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:06.670
I don't quite get it either.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:09.370
Kana alone is already cumbersome as she is.

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:11.390
Is this combustible trash?

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.100
It's not combustible.

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:16.370
Sorry for troubling you.

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:18.360
No, please feel free to ask questions.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.750
Then what about this one?

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:23.950
Yes, it's non-combustible trash.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:26.840
Thanks, you helped me a lot.

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:28.960
Please feel free to ask questions.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:36.860
Hey, Chiaki. Is this non-combustible trash?

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:39.950
It's obviously combustible. You should know better.

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:43.390
What a cold person.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.360
Use your head more!

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.140
Hey, Chiaki.

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:51.940
What is it now?

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:53.390
I'm tired of it.

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:02.200
Aluminum can.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:11.640
I'm working hard too, Minami Haruka.

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:18.970
It looks like my help isn't needed.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:21.460
Oh, well.

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:23.380
Steel can.

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:32.450
Hey. Don't sleep. Stop slacking off. Stop messing around.

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:35.950
I'll leave the rest to you, my hardworking little sister.

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:38.590
Enough with that. Stand up, you lazy big sister!

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:42.630
Don't get so worked up. Since even if I don't do it, someone else will...

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:43.950
What're you doing, Kana?!
Don't get so worked up. Since even if I don't do it, someone else will...

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:44.320
What're you doing, Kana?!

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:46.650
Haruka-neesama.

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:48.630
I'm tired of it.

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:49.500
You...

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:54.660
If you don't pick up the trash properly, then no dinner for you, understand?!

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:56.160
No way!

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:59.530
Um... Haruka-neesama. Me too?

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:01.430
If you don't want that, then do it properly!

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:05.960
Pinch...

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:07.760
Good job.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:08.700
How did it go?

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:13.380
Look! With this much, we can have a crab feast tonight, right?

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:18.770
Good work, Fuyuki-kun.

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:19.390
It's nothing.

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:23.390
Fuyuki-kun is really formidable. That's already his second bag today.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:28.690
Oh, no, the others have helped me out a lot.

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:30.160
You're too modest.

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:35.510
You... How did you manage to pick up that much?!

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:37.430
Don't you know when to slack off?!

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:44.620
Stop speaking nonsense. You should try to be more diligent like Fuyuki-kun.

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:45.650
Right?

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:47.580
I'm sorry...

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:49.710
Oh my, please don't mind.

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:52.740
Kana just loves to cause a ruckus.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:58.890
Why are you dealing additional damage? You're assisting the attack! It has support effects, okay?

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:00.710
You should learn from Fuyuki-kun.

00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:03.730
Aren't you feeling ashamed as his senior?

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:08.100
Um... I really haven't done anything special.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:12.770
Hey you, you were just praised, so you should be happy.

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:14.370
Eh?

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:15.720
Now, now, Chiaki.

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:18.200
But, Haruka-neesama...

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:21.280
Then I'll take my leave.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:22.810
Do your best.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:29.180
Both of you should do your best too. Don't lose to Fuyuki-kun now.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:35.880
The problem has worsened. If I lose to Fuyuki-kun, then I won't get dinner.

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:38.950
Garbage picking competition?

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:42.290
Would Haruka-san say something so inciting?

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:43.640
What happened, Chiaki?

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:48.430
Well, she did say something about not losing to Fuyuki-kun, but...

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:52.020
It seems even though Haruka looks like that, she doesn't like to lose.

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:54.390
Listen up, everyone!

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:57.150
The situation is just as you've heard. The situation is really serious!

00:13:57.590 --> 00:14:01.820
Whether I get dinner or not will depend on this battle.

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:03.800
I anticipate full effort from everyone!

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:05.110
Huh? Us too?

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:07.910
She already plans to rely on us from the start...

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:10.150
This looks to be problematic...

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:12.130
Just like always.

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:13.340
Is it all right if we don't stop her?

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:17.800
Yeah, even though I'm not sure why, I don't feel like losing to Fuyuki-kun either.

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:20.180
Then let's decide our battle plan!

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:22.290
Keiko the strategist!

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.730
Oh, she said she has something to do in the afternoon, so she left.

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:27.720
That traitor...

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:30.910
Then, Chiaki! Tactics!

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:34.920
It seems the litter at the park has pretty much been cleaned up.

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:36.860
It's unlikely we can win by staying here.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:37.860
Then what should we do?

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:41.370
Let's go some place that's full of litter.

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:48.660
It's sooo cold...

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:51.030
Did we really have to come to such a place...

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:54.290
Look! It's garbage! There's garbage!

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.970
Treasure hunt!

00:14:58.450 --> 00:14:59.670
A soda pop? Nice find!

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:03.690
Whoa, this is incredible.

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:06.080
There's a lot of illegal dumping here.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:07.180
Illegal dumping?

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:12.650
It means throwing out things that are not disposable to places you can't litter.

00:15:12.650 --> 00:15:15.400
What a find, everyone!

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:19.060
We can have unidon for dinner tonight with this much!

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:19.740
Haruka is not going to believe it!

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:23.480
She is throwing away stuff that she as a person shouldn't throw away.
Haruka is not going to believe it!

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:28.820
Chiaki, look.

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:36.190
That guy, he even came here.

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:38.120
He's here to interfere with us again.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:42.250
He's probably some vanguard that was sent by the enemy to steal our dinner.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:45.310
Eh? I don't think that's the way to put it.

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:47.520
It's not dinner, it's garbage...

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:49.370
Is it someone in the same profession as us?

00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:50.320
What profession?

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:51.500
Treasure Hunter.

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:52.950
No! You're totally wrong.

00:15:53.710 --> 00:15:56.480
The transfer student sure is working hard.

00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:58.850
The kind of person that will grow up to be someone important?

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:02.820
He must have gotten so much garbage from being here.

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:06.550
No one would want to come to such a cold place.

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:11.730
Only he would accept a dirty job like that.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.240
So cold...

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:18.930
It's so cold. Let's go back. It doesn't have to be the riverbank, right?

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:23.380
No! Now that we know where the enemy gathers, we have to decide it here once and for all!

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:42.620
Hey, Touma. Check it out!

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:43.040
Huh?

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:44.730
Great, simply great!

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:46.570
Geez. Get serious!

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:17.420
Do you need some help?

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:23.780
Ah, let me help you.

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:28.140
You have to loosen the soil around it.

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:31.400
It's not like I'm asking for your help.

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:32.810
Eh?

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:34.570
Nah, never mind.

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:39.030
Now after I say 3-2-1, we pull!

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:40.560
Understood.

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:43.290
3-2-1, pull!

00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:45.360
Thanks a lot.

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:47.160
Don't mention it.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.430
Um... is something wrong?

00:17:51.430 --> 00:17:54.260
No. I was just wondering whether you find joy in helping others out.

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:00.170
Hey, you there! Can you help me out here?

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:03.990
I feel bad for having you go into the water, but I can't move it by myself.

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:06.710
Is he serious?

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:10.560
Hey, you!

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:12.830
Please!

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:13.970
C–Coming!

00:18:18.400 --> 00:18:23.410
Could it be that... he doesn't know how to refuse others?

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:30.590
No wonder it's so cold...

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:33.130
It really has started snowing.

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:35.400
Please inform all participants that the event's been cancelled.

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:38.890
What the... The forecast said it wouldn't snow until tonight.

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:41.960
There are people by the river. Someone needs to go inform them.

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:44.520
Then I'll go.

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:47.780
Where did Chiaki and the others go?

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:52.900
Hey, Chiaki!

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:54.060
What is it?

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:56.870
Well, you see, Kana...

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:57.410
This way.

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:03.300
What do you think? Amazing, isn't it?

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:08.130
If we bring this back, even Fuyuki will have to accept defeat.

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:10.520
It's impossible to bring such a thing back.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:12.800
That's what I said to her, but...

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:16.540
It won't even budge an inch.

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:19.200
Don't give up already! Where there's a will, there's a way!

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:20.640
It's no good.

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:23.720
Even if we go at it together, it's impossible to carry it all the way from here to the park.

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:25.780
I have an idea.

00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:27.710
Oh? Like what?

00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:29.060
We'll gather some logs.

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:30.830
Logs? And then?

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:33.400
We line them up neatly, and then we roll it onto them.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.030
Can you kill yourself?

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:37.700
The cold weather is making her jabs colder than usual.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:41.200
It's snowing, anyway. Let's go back.

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:43.610
Yeah, let's go back.

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:46.010
I don't want to!

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:48.590
I'll bring it back no matter what.

00:19:48.590 --> 00:19:51.760
Kana-chan! Kana-chan! She can't breathe! She's going to suffocate!

00:19:57.610 --> 00:19:59.930
Maybe there's something inside?

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:02.020
I see. That must be why...

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:05.010
Okay, let's open it.

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:08.100
Eh? It's shut tight.

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:13.270
I've heard stories about people throwing away 100 million yen into the garbage.

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:15.850
For real? Then this is just like a safe.

00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:17.860
It might be a corpse.

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:21.150
Hey, stop it. That even gives me the chills.

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:29.130
If there's really 100 million yen inside then I'll give each of you 10,000 yen to spend however you want.

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:30.240
Look forward to it.

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:31.700
How stingy.

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:36.960
From dinner to 100 million yen. The river of desire sure has swelled.

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:41.510
Just a bit more...

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:44.400
What should I buy?

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:49.070
I can buy a lot of 10 yen chocolate and make a 10 yen chocolate bath. What do you think?

00:20:49.070 --> 00:20:52.890
Well... I think even if it's not 10 yen chocolate, once melted they're all the same.

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:55.810
Good timing. There is just a skirt that I've wanted.

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:00.240
Eh? Uh...

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:04.660
Isn't it a crime to share booty of lost items in the first place?

00:21:07.590 --> 00:21:09.130
You did it!!

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:11.420
100 million yen!

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:13.750
What's this?

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:16.040
Seems like... rocks.

00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:18.100
What's going on?

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:19.240
A prank most likely.

00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:20.460
But for what?

00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:25.720
It's a prank to make a fool out of someone like you who's so greedy that you think something good must be inside,

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:27.940
only to be in utter disappointment after opening it.

00:21:31.280 --> 00:21:33.100
What a tasteless joke!

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:35.410
Scaring us to death!

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:37.730
Got myself all frozen!

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:40.190
I was looking forward to it too!

00:21:47.430 --> 00:21:48.910
What are you guys doing?

00:21:50.300 --> 00:21:52.480
I came here to search for you.

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:57.380
Only to find you guys slacking off and having fun throwing rocks instead.

00:21:57.810 --> 00:22:00.830
Uh... you see... well...

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:03.640
H–Haruka-neesama... We can explain...

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:05.600
No dinner for you two!

00:22:06.120 --> 00:22:08.550
Haruka-neesama!
Haruka!

00:22:37.110 --> 00:22:40.250
I'll clean them up. You can just leave them there.

00:22:41.110 --> 00:22:42.860
No, I'm fine.

00:22:47.070 --> 00:22:47.760
Hey.

00:22:49.210 --> 00:22:52.360
If you don't like doing it, then just flat out refuse.

00:22:54.080 --> 00:22:56.930
Chiaki, hurry up.

00:22:56.930 --> 00:22:58.400
I'm coming now.

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:24.310
What happened, both of you?

00:23:24.310 --> 00:23:26.090
You woke up even earlier than I did.

00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:29.840
Give us food!

00:25:00.300 --> 00:25:03.750
Some people presume that people have nose bleeds because they're hot-blooded.

00:25:03.750 --> 00:25:04.900
That is only superstition, you idiot.

00:25:05.110 --> 00:25:09.150
Most nose bleeds happen as a result of the anterior of the Kiesselbach's area being wounded,

00:25:09.150 --> 00:25:10.570
it'll stop in no time, so don't worry.

00:25:10.820 --> 00:25:14.700
If by chance it doesn't stop then it may be due to sickness, and it's best to visit the hospital.
